### API Testing Example
# You can use VS Code extension "REST Client" to test these APIs
# Or import these concepts to Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1. Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "client"
}

###

### 2. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 3. Get Current User Profile (Requires Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 4. Update Profile (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bio": "I am an experienced client looking for top talent.",
  "skills": ["Project Management", "Agile"]
}

###

### 5. Admin: Get all users
# Only works if the logged-in user is an admin
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
